@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About";
    ViewData["Description"] = "About the Monero User Forum — a private, independent place for Monero users to talk. No email required, works over Tor. Part of the Monerica Network.";
}

<div class="panel" style="text-align:center;">
    <img src="~/img/monerouserforum.png" alt="Monero User Forum" style="width:200px;max-width:70%;border-radius:16px;" />
    <h1 style="margin:12px 0 4px;">About <span class="accent">Monero</span> User Forum</h1>
    <p class="muted" style="max-width:680px;margin:0 auto;">A place for Monero users to communicate.</p>
</div>

<div class="panel">
    <h2 class="panel-title">Our mission</h2>
    <p>
        Monero User Forum exists to give the Monero community a private, independent place to talk —
        about the market, the technology, and everything in between. It's built the way a Monero
        forum should be: <strong>no email required to join</strong>, fully usable <strong>over Tor</strong>,
        and designed to respect your privacy at every step.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
        Members are approved by hand to keep spam out, build a reputation over time, and can talk in
        threads, private messages, and a live chatroom — all under the Monero banner.
    </p>
    <ul class="muted" style="line-height:1.9;padding-left:18px;">
        <li><strong>Price Talk</strong> — markets, trading, and where Monero is headed.</li>
        <li><strong>Technical Help</strong> — wallets, nodes, and troubleshooting.</li>
        <li><strong>General Discussion</strong> — everything else Monero.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:0;">
        Part of the <a asp-action="Network">Monerica Network</a> — a family of independent,
        privacy-focused sites for the Monero community.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="panel">
    <h2 class="panel-title">Privacy &amp; logging</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin-bottom:0;">
        We keep basic activity logs to run and protect the forum, but <strong>we do not log IP
        addresses</strong>. Unique thread views are counted with a random per-browser marker — never
        an IP and nothing that identifies you. Sign-up needs no email, and the site works over Tor.
    </p>
</div>
